    },
    "grade": "9-10",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A sequence of 2017 digits is written. It is known that all two-digit numbers, which consist of two consecutive digits in the sequence (in the order in which they are written) are divisible by 17 or by 23. The last digit in the sequence is 1. What is the first digit in the sequence?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "9"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Work backwards",
        "body": "The two-digit multiples of 17 or 23 are $17, 34, 51, 68, 85$ and $23, 46, 69, 92$. Every digit appears at most once as a **second** digit among them, so going backwards each digit determines the one before it:\n$$1 \\leftarrow 5 \\leftarrow 8 \\leftarrow 6 \\leftarrow 4 \\leftarrow 3 \\leftarrow 2 \\leftarrow 9 \\leftarrow 6 \\leftarrow 4 \\leftarrow \\cdots$$\n(from 51, 85, 68, 46, 34, 23, 92, 69, 46, …). So the sequence ends with $\\ldots 6\\,8\\,5\\,1$, and before the final $8\\,5\\,1$ the block $6, 4, 3, 2, 9$ repeats (read backwards).\n\nPositions 2017, 2016, 2015 hold $1, 5, 8$. Position $2014 - k$ holds the $(k \\bmod 5)$-th entry of $(6, 4, 3, 2, 9)$, counting from 0. Position 1 has $k = 2013$, and $2013 = 5\\cdot402 + 3$, so it holds the entry with index 3, which is $2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 2**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "sequences-series"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
    "id": "kangaroo-ca-2017-g0910-27",
    "bank": "kangaroo",
    "source": {
      "contest": "Canadian Math Kangaroo",
